{
  "title": "16: al-Nahl النحل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاَتٰۤى اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ فَلَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْهُ‌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(1)\nATAA AMRUL LAAHE FALAA TASTAA’JELOOHU WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nAllah's commandment has come, therefore do not desire to hasten it; glory be to Him, and highly exalted be He above what they associate (with Him).\nيُنَزِّلُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةَ بِالرُّوْحِ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖۤ اَنْ اَنْذِرُوْۤا اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(2)\nYUNAZZELU AL-MALAAEKATA BEALRROOHE MIN AMREHI A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI AN AANZEROOA ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FAT-TAQOON.\nHe sends down the angels with the inspiration by His commandment on whom He pleases of His servants, saying: Give the warning that there is no god but Me, therefore be careful (of your duty) to Me.\nخَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ تَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(3)\nKHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ TAA’AALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nHe created the heavens and the earth with the truth, highly exalted be He above what they associate (with Him).\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ فَاِذَا هُوَ خَصِيْمٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(4)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN NUTFATIN FA-EZAA HOWA KHASEEMUM MOBEEN.\nHe created man from a small seed and lo! he is an open contender.\nوَالْاَنْعَامَ خَلَقَهَا‌ ۚ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا دِفْ ٴٌ وَّمَنَافِعُ وَمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWAL AANA’AAMA KHALAQAHAA LAKUM FEEHAA DEF UN WA MANAA-FE-O’ WA MINHAA TAAKULOONA.\nAnd He created the cattle for you; you have in them warm clothing and (many) advantages, and of them do you eat.\nوَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا جَمَالٌ حِيْنَ تُرِيْحُوْنَ وَحِيْنَ تَسْرَحُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA LAKUM FEEHAA JAMAALUN HEENA TUREEHOONA WA TASRAHOONA.\nAnd there is beauty in them for you when you drive them back (to home), and when you send them forth (to pasture).\nوَتَحْمِلُ اَثْقَالَكُمْ اِلٰى بَلَدٍ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا بٰلِغِيْهِ اِلَّا بِشِقِّ الْاَنْفُسِ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكُمْ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ‏(7)\nWA TAHMELO AASQAALAKUM ELAA BALADIN LAM TAKOONOO BAALEGHEEHE ILLAA BESHEQQE AL-AANFUSE INNAL TAQUL LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nAnd they carry your heavy loads to regions which you could not reach but with distress of the souls; most surely your Lord is Compassionate, Merciful.\nوَّالْخَيْلَ وَالْبِغَالَ وَالْحَمِيْرَ لِتَرْكَبُوْهَا وَزِيْنَةً‌ ؕ وَيَخْلُقُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(8)\nWWAALKHAYLA WAL BEGHAALA WAL HAMEERA LETARKABOOHAA WAZEENATAN WA YAKHLOQO MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd (He made) horses and mules and asses that you might ride upon them and as an ornament; and He creates what you do not know.\nوَعَلَى اللّٰهِ قَصْدُ السَّبِيْلِ وَمِنْهَا جَآئِرٌ‌ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ لَهَدٰٮكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(9)\nWA LAAHE QASDU SABEELE WA MINHAA JAAERUN WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAHADAAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nAnd upon Allah it rests to show the right way, and there are some deviating (ways); and if He please He would certainly guide you all aright.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً‌ لَّكُمْ مِّنْهُ شَرَابٌ وَّمِنْهُ شَجَرٌ فِيْهِ تُسِيْمُوْنَ‏(10)\nHOWA LAZEE ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN LAKUM MINHO SHARAABUN WWAMENHU SHAJARUN FEEHE TUSEEMOONA.\nHe it is Who sends down water from the cloud for you; it gives drink, and by it (grow) the trees upon which you pasture.\nيُنْۢبِتُ لَكُمْ بِهِ الزَّرْعَ وَالزَّيْتُوْنَ وَالنَّخِيْلَ وَالْاَعْنَابَ وَمِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(11)\nYUNBETU LAKUM BEHIL AZ-ZARA’A WAALZZAYTOONA WAALNNAKHEELA WAL AAA’NAABA WA MIN KULLE AS-SAMARAATE INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nHe causes to grow for you thereby herbage, and the olives, and the palm trees, and the grapes, and of all the fruits; most surely there is a sign in this for a people who reflect.\nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَۙ وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ‌ؕ وَالنُّجُوْمُ مُسَخَّرٰتٌۢ بِاَمْرِهٖؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَۙ‏(12)\nSAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA WA SHAMSA WAL QAMARA WA NOJOOMUN MUSAKKHARAATUN BEAAMREH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd He has made subservient for you the night and the day and the sun and the moon, and the stars are made subservient by His commandment; most surely there are signs in this for a people who ponder;\nوَمَا ذَرَاَ لَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُخْتَلِفًا اَلْوَانُهٗ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA MAA ZARAALAKUM FIL ARZE MUKHTALEFAN AALWAANUH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YYAZZAKKAROONA.\nAnd what He has created in the earth of varied hues most surely there is a sign in this for a people who are mindful.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ سَخَّرَ الْبَحْرَ لِتَاْكُلُوْا مِنْهُ لَحْمًا طَرِيًّا وَّتَسْتَخْرِجُوْا مِنْهُ حِلْيَةً تَلْبَسُوْنَهَا‌ۚ وَتَرَى الْفُلْكَ مَوَاخِرَ فِيْهِ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA HOWA LAZEE SAKKHARA BAHRA LE-TAAKOLOO MINHO SUMMA NAKSOOHAA TAREEA WWATASTAKHREJOOA MINHO HELYATAN TALBASOONAHAA WA TARAL AL-FULKA MAWAAKHERA FEEHE WA LETABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd He it is Who has made the sea subservient that you may eat fresh flesh from it and bring forth from it ornaments which you wear, and you see the ships cleaving through it, and that you might seek of His bounty and that you may give thanks.\nوَاَلْقٰى فِى الْاَرْضِ رَوَاسِىَ اَنْ تَمِيْدَ بِكُمْ وَاَنْهٰرًا وَّسُبُلًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَۙ‏(15)\nWAALQAA FIL ARZE JA-A’LA AN TAMEEDA BEKUM WA KHELAALAHAA WWASUBULAN LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\nAnd He has cast great mountains in the earth lest it might be convulsed with you, and rivers and roads that you may go aright,\nوَعَلٰمٰتٍ‌ؕ وَبِالنَّجْمِ هُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(16)\nWAA’ALAAMAATIN WABEALNNAJME HUM YAHTADOON.\nAnd landmarks; and by the stars they find the right way.\nاَفَمَنْ يَّخْلُقُ كَمَنْ لَّا يَخْلُقُ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(17)\nAFAMAWN YYAKHLUQU KAMAM LAA YAKHLUQU AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nIs He then Who creates like him who does not create? Do you not then mind?\nوَاِنْ تَعُدُّوْا نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ لَا تُحْصُوْهَاؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(18)\nWA TAU’UDDOOA NE’MATAL LAAHE LAA TUHSOOHAA INNAL LAAHA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nAnd if you would count Allah's favors, you will not be able to number them; most surely Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُسِرُّوْنَ وَ مَا تُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(19)\nWAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TUSERROONA WA MAA MAA TO’LENOON.\nAnd Allah knows what you conceal and what you do openly.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَا يَخْلُقُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَؕ‏(20)\nWAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAA YAKHLUQOONA SHAY-ANW WA HUM YUKHLAQOONA.\nAnd those whom they call on besides Allah have not created anything while they are themselves created;\nاَمْوَاتٌ غَيْرُ اَحْيَآءٍ‌ ۚ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(21)\nAMWAAT GHAYRO AAHYAAIN WA MAA YASH-O’ROON AYYAANA YUB-A’SOON.\nDead (are they), not living, and they know not when they shall be raised.\nاِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌‌ ۚ فَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ مُّنْكِرَةٌ وَّهُمْ مُّسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(22)\nELAAHOKUM ELAAHUN WAAHED FAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE QULOOBUHUM MMUNKERATUN WA HUM HUM MUSTAKBEROON.\nYour Allah is one Allah; so (as for) those who do not believe in the hereafter, their hearts are ignorant and they are proud.\nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْتَكْبِرِيْنَ‏(23)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA YUA’LENOONA INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL AL-MUSTAKBEREENA.\nTruly Allah knows what they hide and what they manifest; surely He does not love the proud.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ مَّاذَاۤ اَنْزَلَ رَبُّكُمْ‌ۙ قَالُوْۤا اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(24)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM MMAAZAA ANZALAL RABBOKUM QAALOO ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nAnd when it is said to them, what is it that your Lord has revealed? They say: Stories of the ancients;\nلِيَحْمِلُوْۤا اَوْزَارَهُمْ كَامِلَةً يَّوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ۙ وَمِنْ اَوْزَارِ الَّذِيْنَ يُضِلُّوْنَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ‌ؕ اَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَزِرُوْنَ‏(25)\nLEEHMELOOA AAWZAARAHUM KAAMELATAN YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA MIN AAWZAARE LAZEENA YUZELLOONAHUM BEGHAYRIL E’ELMIN ALAA SAAA-A MAA YAZEROONA.\nThat they may bear their burdens entirely on the day of resurrection and also of the burdens of those whom they lead astray without knowledge; now surely evil is what they bear.\nقَدْ مَكَرَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَاَتَى اللّٰهُ بُنْيَانَهُمْ مِّنَ الْقَوَاعِدِ فَخَرَّ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّقْفُ مِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَاَتٰٮهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(26)\nQAD MAKARA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FAATAA LAAHO BUNYAANAHUM MENAL AL-QAWAAE’EDE FAKHARRA A’LAYHEMUL AS-SAQFU MIN FAWQEHIM WAATAAHUMU A’ZAABO MIN HAYSO LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThose before them did indeed devise plans, but Allah demolished their building from the foundations, so the roof fell down on them from above them, and the punishment came to them from whence they did not perceive.\nثُمَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يُخْزِيْهِمْ وَيَقُوْلُ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تُشَآقُّوْنَ فِيْهِمْ‌ؕ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ اِنَّ الْخِزْىَ الْيَوْمَ وَالسُّوْۤءَ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَۙ‏(27)\nSUMMA YAWMA QEYAAMATE YUKHZEEHEM WA YAQOOLO AYNA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA KUNTUM TUSHAAQQOONA FEEHEM QAALA LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA INNAL AL-KHEZAAA YAWMA WAALSSOOA A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nThen on the resurrection day He will bring them to disgrace and say: Where are the associates you gave Me, for whose sake you became hostile? Those who are given the knowledge will say: Surely the disgrace and the evil are this day upon the unbelievers:\nالَّذِيْنَ تَتَوَفّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ ظَالِمِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ‌ فَاَلْقَوُا السَّلَمَ مَا كُنَّا نَعْمَلُ مِنْ سُوْۤءٍؕ بَلٰٓى اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(28)\nLAZEENA TATAWAFFAAHUMU AL-MALAAEKATU ZAALEMEAA ANFOSEHIM FAALQAWUA AS-SALAMA MAA KUNNAA NAA’MALU MIN SOOIN BALAAA INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThose whom the angels cause to die while they are unjust to themselves. Then would they offer submission: We used not to do any evil. Aye! surely Allah knows what you did.\nفَادْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ؕ فَلَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(29)\nEZAA AABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA FALABESA MASWAA AL-MUTAKABBEREENA.\nTherefore enter the gates of hell, to abide therein; so certainly evil is the dwelling place of the proud.\nوَقِيْلَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا مَاذَاۤ اَنْزَلَ رَبُّكُمْ‌ؕ قَالُوْا خَيْرًاؕ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةٌ‌  ؕ وَلَدَارُ الْاٰخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ ‌ ؕ وَلَنِعْمَ دَارُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(30)\nWA QEELAD LILLAZEENA TAQAW MAA ANZALAL RABBUKUM QAALOO KHAYRAN LIL-LAZEENA AAHSANOOA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA HASANATUL WALADAARU AAKHERATE KHAYRUL WALANEA’MA DAARU MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd it is said to those who guard (against evil): What is it that your Lord has revealed? They say, Good. For those who do good in this world is good, and certainly the abode of the hereafter is better; and certainly most excellent is the abode of those who guard (against evil);\nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ يَّدْخُلُوْنَهَا تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ‌ لَهُمْ فِيْهَا مَا يَشَآءُوْنَ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَجْزِى اللّٰهُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(31)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN YYADKHULOONAHAA TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO LAHUM FEEHAA MAA YASHAAOONA KAZAALEKA YAJZEAA LAAHO MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nThe gardens of perpetuity, they shall enter them, rivers flowing beneath them; they shall have in them what they please. Thus does Allah reward those who guard (against evil),\nالَّذِيْنَ تَتَوَفّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ طَيِّبِيْنَ‌ ۙ يَقُوْلُوْنَ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمُۙ ادْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(32)\nLAZEENA TATAWAFFAAHUMU AL-MALAAEKATU TAYBEENA YAQOOLOONA SALAAMUN A’LAYKOMUL ADKHULOOA JANNATA BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThose whom the angels cause to die in a good state, saying: Peace be on you: enter the garden for what you did.\nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ اَوْ يَاْتِىَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ فَعَلَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ؕ وَمَا ظَلَمَهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(33)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA AN TAA-TEYAHOMUL AL-MALAAEKATU AW HATTAA AMRUL RABBEKA KAZAALEKA FA-A’LA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA MAA ZALAMAHUMU LAAHO WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nThey do not wait aught but that the angels should come to them or that the commandment of your Lord should come to pass. Thus did those before them; and Allah was not unjust to them, but they were unjust to themselves.\nفَاَصَابَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(34)\nFAASAABAHUM SAYAAATU MAA A’MELOO WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nSo the evil (consequences) of what they did shall afflict them and that which they mocked shall encompass them.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا لَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا عَبَدْنَا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ شَىْءٍ نَّحْنُ وَلَاۤ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَلَا حَرَّمْنَا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ فَعَلَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ۚ فَهَلْ عَلَى الرُّسُلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(35)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA ASHRAKOO LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA A’ABADNAA MIN DOONEHI MIN SHAY-IN NNAHNU WA LAA AAABAAUNAA WA LAA HARRAMNAA MIN DOONEHI MIN SHAYIN KAZAALEKA FA-A’LA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA HAL A’LAL AR-RUSULE ILLAA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nAnd they who give associates (to Allah) say: If Allah had pleased, we would not have served anything besides Allah, (neither) we nor our fathers, nor would we have prohibited anything without (order from) Him. Thus did those before them; is then aught incumbent upon the apostles except a plain delivery (of the message)?\nوَلَقَدْ بَعَثْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ رَّسُوْلًا اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَاجْتَنِبُوا الطَّاغُوْتَ‌ۚ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ هَدَى اللّٰهُ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ حَقَّتْ عَلَيْهِ الضَّلٰلَةُ‌ ؕ فَسِيْرُوْا فِىْ الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(36)\nWA LAQAD BAA’ASNAA FEE KULLE UMMATIN RASOOLANY SAALEHAN BODUL LAAHA WAAJTANEBOOA AT-TAAGHOOTA FA-MINHUM MAN LAZEENA LAAHO WA MINHUM MAN HAQQAT A’LAYHE AZ-ZALAALATU FA SEEROO FEE ARZE FANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MOKAZZEBEENAZ.\nAnd certainly We raised in every nation an apostle saying: Serve Allah and shun the Shaitan. So there were some of them whom Allah guided and there were others against whom error was due; therefore travel in the land, then see what was the end of the rejecters.\nاِنْ تَحْرِصْ عَلٰى هُدٰٮهُمْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يُّضِلُّ‌ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(37)\nIN TAHRES A’LAA HODAAHUM WA FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN YYUZELLU WA MAA LAHUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nIf you desire for their guidance, yet surely Allah does not guide him who leads astray, nor shall they have any helpers.\nوَ اَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ‌ۙ لَا يَبْعَثُ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّمُوْتُ‌ؕ بَلٰى وَعْدًا عَلَيْهِ حَقًّا وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(38)\nWA AAQSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM LAA YABA’ASU LAAHO MAN YYAMOOTU BALAA WA’DAN A’LAYHE HAQQAN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd they swear by Allah with the most energetic of their oaths: Allah will not raise up him who dies. Yea! it is a promise binding on Him, quite true, but most people do not know;\nلِيُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ الَّذِىْ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ فِيْهِ وَ لِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(39)\nLEEBAYNA LAHOMUL LAZEE YAKHTALEFOON FEEHE WA LEEA’LAMA LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAHUM KAANOO KAAZEBEENA.\nSo that He might make manifest to them that about which they differ, and that those who disbelieve might know that they were liars.\nاِنَّمَا قَوْلُنَا لِشَىْءٍ اِذَاۤ اَرَدْنٰهُ اَنْ نَّقُوْلَ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(40)\nINNAMAA QAWLUNAA LE-SHAY-IN EZAA AARADNAAHU AN NNAQOOLA LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nOur word for a thing when We intend it, is only that We say to it, Be, and it is.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا فِى اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوْا لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً‌  ؕ وَلَاَجْرُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ‌ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(41)\nWAL LAZEENA HAAJAROO FIL LAAHE MIN BA’DE MAA ZULEMOOA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FIL DUNYAA HASANATANW WALAAJRU AAKHERATE AKBARO LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nAnd those who fly for Allah's sake after they are oppressed, We will most certainly give them a good abode in the world, and the reward of the hereafter is certainly much greater, did they but know;\nالَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ‏(42)\nLAZEENA SABAROO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nThose who are patient and on their Lord do they rely.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ اِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ‌ فَسْئَلُوْۤا اَهْلَ الذِّكْرِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(43)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA ILLAA REJAALAN NNOOHEAA ELAYHIM FASALOOA AHLAL AZ-ZEKRE IN KUNTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd We did not send before you any but men to whom We sent revelation-- so ask the followers of the Reminder if you do not know--\nبِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالزُّبُرِ‌ؕ وَاَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الذِّكْرَ لِتُبَيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ مَا نُزِّلَ اِلَيْهِمْ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(44)\nBIL-BAYYENAATE WAALZZUBURE WA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KHASEYAR LETUBAYNA LIN-NAASE MAA NUZZELA ELAYHIM WA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAFAKKAROON.\nWith clear arguments and scriptures; and We have revealed to you the Reminder that you may make clear to men what has been revealed to them, and that haply they may reflect.\nاَفَاَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ مَكَرُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ يَّخْسِفَ اللّٰهُ بِهِمُ الْاَرْضَ اَوْ يَاْتِيَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(45)\nAAFAAMENA LAZEENA MAKAROOA SAYYE-AATE AN YAKHSEFA LAAHO BEHEMUL ARZA AW YAATEEHUMU A’ZAABO MIN HAYSO LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nDo they then who plan evil (deeds) feel secure (of this) that Allah will not cause the earth to swallow them or that punishment may not overtake them from whence they do not perceive?\nاَوْ يَاْخُذَهُمْ فِىْ تَقَلُّبِهِمْ فَمَا هُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَۙ‏(46)\nAW YAAKHUZAHUM FEE TAQALLUBEHEM FAMAA HUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nOr that He may not seize them in the course of their journeys, then shall they not escape;\nاَوْ يَاْخُذَهُمْ عَلٰى تَخَوُّفٍؕ فَاِنَّ رَبَّكُمْ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(47)\nAW YAAKHUZAHUM A’LAA TAKHAWFIN FA-INNAL TAQUL LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nOr that He may not seize them by causing them to suffer gradual loss, for your Lord is most surely Compassionate, Merciful.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلٰى مَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ يَّتَفَيَّؤُا ظِلٰلُهٗ عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَالشَّمَآئِلِ سُجَّدًا لِّلَّهِ وَهُمْ دٰخِرُوْنَ‏(48)\nAWALAM YARAW ELAA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO MIN SHAY-IN YYATAFAYUA ZELAALUH A’NIL YAMEENE WAALSSHAMAAELE SUJJADANW LILLAAH WA HUM DAAKHEROONA.\nDo they not consider every thing that Allah has created? Its (very) shadows return from right and left, making obeisance to Allah while they are in utter abasement.\nوَلِلّٰهِ يَسْجُدُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ وَّالْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(49)\nLILLAAHE YASJUDU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE MIN DAAAB-BATIL WWAALMALAAEKATU WA HUM LAA YASTAKBEROONA.\nAnd whatever creature that is in the heavens and that is in the earth makes obeisance to Allah (only), and the angels (too) and they do not show pride.\nيَخَافُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ مِّنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَيَفْعَلُوْنَ مَا يُؤْمَرُوْنَ ۩‏(50)\nYAKHAAFOONA RABBAHUM MIN FAWQEHIM WA YAF-A’LOON MAA YUMAROONA.\nThey fear their Lord above them and do what they are commanded.\nوَقَالَ اللّٰهُ لَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اِلٰهَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ‌ۚ اِنَّمَا هُوَ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌ ۚ فَاِيَّاىَ فَارْهَبُوْنِ‏(51)\nWA QAALA LAAHO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AELAAHAYNE NAYNE INNAMAA HOWA ELAAHUN WAAHED FA-IYYAA-YA FARHABOON.\nAnd Allah has said: Take not two gods, He is only one Allah; so of Me alone should you be afraid.\nوَلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ وَلَهُ الدِّيْنُ وَاصِبًا‌ ؕ اَفَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA ARZE LAHUL DEENO WAASEBAN AAFAGHAYRA LAAHE TATTAQOON.\nAnd whatever is in the heavens and the earth is His, and to Him should obedience be (rendered) constantly; will you then guard against other than (the punishment of) Allah?\nوَمَا بِكُمْ مِّنْ نِّعْمَةٍ فَمِنَ اللّٰهِ‌ ثُمَّ اِذَا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فَاِلَيْهِ تَجْئَرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nWA MAA BEKUM MIN NEA’MATIN NAASE LAAHE SUMMA EZAA MASSAKUMU AZ-ZURRU FA ELAYHE TAJAROONA.\nAnd whatever favor is (bestowed) on you it is from Allah; then when evil afflicts you, to Him do you cry for aid.\nثُمَّ اِذَا كَشَفَ الضُّرَّ عَنْكُمْ اِذَا فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْكُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(54)\nSUMMA EZAA KASHAFA AZ-ZURRA A’NKUM EZAA FAREEQUM MINKUM BE-RABBEHIM YUSHREKOON.\nYet when He removes the evil from you, lo! a party of you associate others with their Lord;\nلِيَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ فَتَمَتَّعُوْا‌ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(55)\nLE-YAKFOROO BEMAA AATAYNAAHUM FATAMATTAO’O FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nSo that they be ungrateful for what We have given them; then enjoy yourselves; for soon will you know\nوَيَجْعَلُوْنَ لِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ نَصِيْبًا مِّمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ تَاللّٰهِ لَتُسْئَلُنَّ عَمَّا كُنْتُمْ تَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(56)\nWA YAJ-A’LOONA LEMAKH LAA YA’LAMOON NASEEBAN MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM TAALLLAAHE LA-TUS-A-LUNNA A’MMAA KUNTUM TAFTAROONA.\nAnd they set apart for what they do not know a portion of what We have given them. By Allah, you shall most certainly be questioned about that which you forged.\nوَيَجْعَلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ الْبَنٰتِ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ۙ وَلَهُمْ مَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَ‏(57)\nWA YAJ-A’LOONA LILLAAHE AL-BANAATE WALADAN WA LAHUM MAA YASHTAHOONA.\nAnd they ascribe daughters to Allah, glory be to Him; and for themselves (they would have) what they desire.\nوَاِذَا بُشِّرَ اَحَدُهُمْ بِالْاُنْثٰى ظَلَّ وَجْهُهٗ مُسْوَدًّا وَّهُوَ كَظِيْمٌ‌ۚ‏(58)\nWA EZAA BUSSHERA AHADOHUM BIL-AUNSAA ZALLA WAJHUH MUSWADDAN WA KAZEEMUN.\nAnd when a daughter is announced to one of them his face becomes black and he is full of wrath.\nيَتَوَارٰى مِنَ الْقَوْمِ مِنْ سُوْۤءِ مَا بُشِّرَ بِهٖ ؕ اَيُمْسِكُهٗ عَلٰى هُوْنٍ اَمْ يَدُسُّهٗ فِى التُّرَابِ‌ ؕ اَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(59)\nYATAWAARAA MENAL QAWMIL MIN SOOE MAA BUSSHERA BEHI AAYUMSEKUH A’LAA HOONIN AM YADUSSUH FIL AT-TURAABE ALAA SAAA-A MAA YAHKUMOONA.\nHe hides himself from the people because of the evil of that which is announced to him. Shall he keep it with disgrace or bury it (alive) in the dust? Now surely evil is what they judge.\nلِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ مَثَلُ السَّوْءِ‌ۚ وَلِلّٰهِ الْمَثَلُ الْاَعْلٰى‌ ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(60)\nLILLAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE MASALUL SAW LILLAAHE MASALUL A-A’LAA WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nFor those who do not believe in the hereafter is an evil attribute, and Allah's is the loftiest attribute; and He is the Mighty, the Wise.\nوَلَوْ يُؤَاخِذُ اللّٰهُ النَّاسَ بِظُلْمِهِمْ مَّا تَرَكَ عَلَيْهَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ وَّلٰكِنْ يُّؤَخِّرُهُمْ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌‌ۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ سَاعَةً‌ وَّلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA LAW YUAAKHEZU LAAHO NAASA BEZULMEHEM MAA TARAKA A’LAYHAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL LAAKIL YYUAKKHERUHUM ELAA ELAA AJALIM FA-EZAA JAAA-A AAJALUHUM LAA YASTAAKHEROONA SAAA’ATAN WA LAA YASTAQDEMOONA.\nAnd if Allah had destroyed men for their iniquity, He would not leave on the earth a single creature, but He respites them till an appointed time; so when their doom will come they shall not be able to delay (it) an hour nor can they bring (it) on (before its time).\nوَيَجْعَلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ مَا يَكْرَهُوْنَ وَتَصِفُ اَلْسِنَتُهُمُ الْكَذِبَ اَنَّ لَهُمُ الْحُسْنٰى‌ؕ لَا جَرَمَ اَنَّ لَهُمُ النَّارَ وَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّفْرَطُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA YAJ-A’LOONA LILLAAHE MAA YAKRAHOONA WATASEFU AALSENATUHUMU AL-KAZEBA ANNAL LAHOMUL HUSNAA LAA JARAMA ANNAL LAHOMUL NAARAL WA ANNAHUM MMUFRATOONA.\nAnd they ascribe to Allah what they (themselves) hate and their tongues relate the lie that they shall have the good; there is no avoiding it that for them is the fire and that they shall be sent before.\nتَاللّٰهِ لَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَهُوَ وَلِيُّهُمُ الْيَوْمَ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(63)\nTAALLLAAHE LAQAD ARSALNAA ELAA OMAMIN MIN QABLEKA FAZAYNA LAHOMUL SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM FAHOWA WALEEHUMU YAWMA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nBy Allah, most certainly We sent (apostles) to nations before you, but the Shaitan made their deeds fair-seeming to them, so he is their guardian today, and they shall have a painful punishment.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ اِلَّا لِتُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ الَّذِى اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ‌ۙ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA MAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABA ILLAA LETUBAYNA LAHOMUL LAZIS TALAFOO FEEHE WA HODANW WA RAHMATAL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nAnd We have not revealed to you the Book except that you may make clear to them that about which they differ, and (as) a guidance and a mercy for a people who believe.\nوَاللّٰهُ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ‏(65)\nWAL LAAHO ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA WA INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YASMA-O’ON.\nAnd Allah has sent down water from the cloud and therewith given life to the earth after its death; most surely there is a sign in this for a people who would listen.\nوَاِنَّ لَكُمْ فِىْ الْاَنْعَامِ لَعِبْرَةً‌  ؕ نُّسْقِيْكُمْ مِّمَّا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهٖ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ فَرْثٍ وَّدَمٍ لَّبَنًا خَالِصًا سَآئِغًا لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ‏(66)\nWA INNA LAKUM FEE AL-AANA’AAME LAE’EBRATAN NNUSQEEKUM MIMMAA FEE BUTOONEH MIN BAYNE FARSIN WWADAMIN LLABANAN KHAALESAN SAAEGHAN LLELSSHAAREBEENA.\nAnd most surely there is a lesson for you in the cattle; We give you to drink of what is in their bellies-- from betwixt the feces and the blood-- pure milk, easy and agreeable to swallow for those who drink.\nوَمِنْ ثَمَرٰتِ النَّخِيْلِ وَالْاَعْنَابِ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مِنْهُ سَكَرًا وَّرِزْقًا حَسَنًا ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA MIN SAMARAATE AN-NAKHEELE WAL AAA’NAABE TATTAKHEZOONA MINHO SAKARAN WWAREZQAN HASANAN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd of the fruits of the palms and the grapes-- you obtain from them intoxication and goodly provision; most surely there is a sign in this for a people who ponder.\nوَاَوْحٰى رَبُّكَ اِلَى النَّحْلِ اَنِ اتَّخِذِىْ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا وَّمِنَ الشَّجَرِ وَمِمَّا يَعْرِشُوْنَۙ‏(68)\nWAAWHAA RABBOKA ELAL AN-NAHLE SAALEHAN ATTAKHEZEAA MENAL JEBAALE BUYOOTAN WWAMENA ASH-SHAJARE WA MIMMAA YAA’RESHOONA.\nAnd your Lord revealed to the bee saying: Make hives in the mountains and in the trees and in what they build:\nثُمَّ كُلِىْ مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ فَاسْلُكِىْ سُبُلَ رَبِّكِ ذُلُلًا‌ ؕ يَخْرُجُ مِنْۢ بُطُوْنِهَا شَرَابٌ مُّخْتَلِفٌ اَلْوَانُهٗ فِيْهِ شِفَآءٌ لِّلنَّاسِ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(69)\nSUMMA KULEAA MIN KULLE SAMARAATE FAASLUKEAA SUBULA RABBEKE ZULULAN YAKHROJO MIN BUTOONEHAA SHARAABUN MMUKHTALEFUN AALWAANUH FEEHE SHEFAAUN LLELNNAASE INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nThen eat of all the fruits and walk in the ways of your Lord submissively. There comes forth from within it a beverage of many colours, in which there is healing for men; most surely there is a sign in this for a people who reflect.\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ ثُمَّ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ‌ۙ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّرَدُّ اِلٰٓى اَرْذَلِ الْعُمُرِ لِكَىْ لَا يَعْلَمَ بَعْدَ عِلْمٍ شَيْئًا‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ قَدِيْرٌ‏(70)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAKUM SUMMA YATAWAFFAAKUM WA MINKUM MAN YYURADDU ELAA AARZALE AL-U’UMURE LEKAY LAA YAA’LAMA BA’DA I’LMIN SHAYAN INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM QADEER.\nAnd Allah has created you, then He causes you to die, and of you is he who is brought back to the worst part of life, so that after having knowledge he does not know anything; surely Allah is Knowing, Powerful.\nوَاللّٰهُ فَضَّلَ بَعْضَكُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فِى الرِّزْقِ‌ۚ فَمَا الَّذِيْنَ فُضِّلُوْا بِرَآدِّىْ رِزْقِهِمْ عَلٰى مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَهُمْ فِيْهِ سَوَآءٌ‌ ؕ اَفَبِنِعْمَةِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(71)\nWAL LAAHO FAZZALA BAA’ZAKUM A’LAA ELAA FIL AR-REZQE FAMAA LAZEENA FUZZELOOA BERAADDEAA REZQEHEM A’LAA MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOHUM FAHUM FEEHE SAWAAA-UN AAFABENEA’MATE LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nAnd Allah has made some of you excel others in the means of subsistence, so those who are made to excel do not give away their sustenance to those whom their right hands possess so that they should be equal therein; is it then the favor of Allah which they deny?\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا وَّ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَزْوَاجِكُمْ بَنِيْنَ وَحَفَدَةً وَّرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ‌ؕ اَفَبِالْبَاطِلِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَبِنِعْمَتِ اللّٰهِ هُمْ يَكْفُرُوْنَۙ‏(72)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN ANFOSEKUM AZWAAJANW WA JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN AAZWAAJEKUM BANEENA WAHAFADATAN WWARAZAQAKUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE AFA-BIL-BAATELE YOAMENOONA WABENEA’MATE LAAHE HUM YAKFOROON.\nAnd Allah has made wives for you from among yourselves, and has given you sons and grandchildren from your wives, and has given you of the good things; is it then in the falsehood that they believe while it is in the favor of Allah that they disbelieve?\nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ رِزْقًا مِّنَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(73)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAMLEKU LAHUM RIZQAN MENAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE SHAY-ANW WA LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA.\nAnd they serve besides Allah that which does not control for them any sustenance at all from the heavens and the earth, nor have they any power.\nفَلَا تَضْرِبُوْا لِلّٰهِ الْاَمْثَالَ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(74)\nFALAA TAZREBOOA LILLAAHE AL-AAMSAALA INNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO WA ANTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nTherefore do not give likenesses to Allah; surely Allah knows and you do not know.\nضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا عَبْدًا مَّمْلُوْكًا لَّا يَقْدِرُ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ وَّمَنْ رَّزَقْنٰهُ مِنَّا رِزْقًا حَسَنًا فَهُوَ يُنْفِقُ مِنْهُ سِرًّا وَّجَهْرًا‌ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوٗنَ‌ؕ اَ لْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(75)\nZARABA LAAHO MASALAA A’BDAN MMAMLOOKAN LAA YAQDERU A’LAA SHAY-IN WWAMAN RRAZAQNAAHU MINNAA RIZQAN HASANAN FAHOWA YUNFEQO MINHO SIRRAN WWAJAHRAN HAL YASTAWNA AALHAMDU LIL-LAAH BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAllah sets forth a parable: (consider) a slave, the property of another, (who) has no power over anything, and one whom We have granted from Ourselves a goodly sustenance so he spends from it secretly and openly; are the two alike? (All) praise is due to Allah! Nay, most of them do not know.\nوَضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلاً رَّجُلَيْنِ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اَبْكَمُ لَا يَقْدِرُ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ كَلٌّ عَلٰى مَوْلٰٮهُۙ اَيْنَمَا يُوَجِّههُّ لَا يَاْتِ بِخَيْرٍ‌ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِىْ هُوَۙ وَمَنْ يَّاْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ‌ۙ وَهُوَ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(76)\nWA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAAN RRAJULAYNE AAHADUHUMAA AABKAMU LAA YAQDERU A’LAA SHAY-IN WA KALLUN A’LAA MAWLAAHU AYNAMAA YOOJJEHHHU LAA TAKOONOO BEKHAYRIN HAL YASTAWEE HOWA WA MAN YYAAMURU BIL-A’DL WA HOWA A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd Allah sets forth a parable of two men; one of them is dumb, not able to do anything, and he is a burden to his master; wherever he sends him, he brings no good; can he be held equal with him who enjoins what is just, and he (himself) is on the right path?\nوَلِلّٰهِ غَيْبُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَمَاۤ اَمْرُ السَّاعَةِ اِلَّا كَلَمْحِ الْبَصَرِ اَوْ هُوَ اَقْرَبُ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(77)\nLILLAAHE GHAYBU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA MAA AMRUL AS-SAAA’ATE ILLAA KALAMHE AL-BASARE AW HOWA AAQRABU INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd Allah's is the unseen of the heavens and the earth; and the matter of the hour is but as the twinkling of an eye or it is higher still; surely Allah has power over all things.\nوَاللّٰهُ اَخْرَجَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا ۙ وَّ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصٰرَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ‌ ۙ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(78)\nWAL LAAHO AAKHRAJAKUM MIN BUTOONE MINHUNNA LAA TA’LAMOON SHAY-ANW WA JA-A’LA LAKOMUL JA-A’LA WAL AABSAARA WA ABSAARA WAL LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd Allah has brought you forth from the wombs of your mothers-- you did not know anything-- and He gave you hearing and sight and hearts that you may give thanks.\nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلَى الطَّيْرِ مُسَخَّرٰتٍ فِىْ جَوِّ السَّمَآءِ ؕ مَا يُمْسِكُهُنَّ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(79)\nALAM YARAW ELAL TAYRE MUSAKKHARAATIN FEE JAW SAMAAA-E MAA YUMSEKOHUNNA ILLAA LAAH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nDo they not see the birds, constrained in the middle of the sky? None withholds them but Allah; most surely there are signs in this for a people who believe.\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بُيُوْتِكُمْ سَكَنًا وَّجَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ جُلُوْدِ الْاَنْعَامِ بُيُوْتًا تَسْتَخِفُّوْنَهَا يَوْمَ ظَعْنِكُمْ وَيَوْمَ اِقَامَتِكُمْ‌ۙ وَمِنْ اَصْوَافِهَا وَاَوْبَارِهَا وَاَشْعَارِهَاۤ اَثَاثًا وَّمَتَاعًا اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(80)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN BUYOOTEKUM SAKANAN ANHAARAWN LAKUM MIN JULOODE AL-AANA’AAME BUYOOTAN TASTAKHEFFOONAHAA YAWMA ZAA’NEKUM WA YAWMA AEQAAMATEKUM WA MIN AASWAAFEHAA WAAWBAAREHAA WAASHA’AAREHAA AASAASAN WA MATAA-A’L ELAA HEEN.\nAnd Allah has given you a place to abide in your houses, and He has given you tents of the skins of cattle which you find light to carry on the day of your march and on the day of your halting, and of their wool and their fur and their hair (He has given you) household stuff and a provision for a time.\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّمَّا خَلَقَ ظِلٰلًا وَّجَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الْجِبَالِ اَكْنَانًا وَّجَعَلَ لَكُمْ سَرَابِيْلَ تَقِيْكُمُ الْحَرَّ وَسَرَابِيْلَ تَقِيْكُمْ بَاْسَكُمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(81)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKUM MIMMAA KHALAQAL ZELAALAN ANHAARAWN LAKUM MENAL JEBAALE AAKNAANAN ANHAARAWN LAKUM SARAABEELA TAQEEKUMU AL-HARRA WASARAABEELA TAQEEKUM BAASAKUM KAZAALEKA YUTEMMU NE’MATAHU A’LAYKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TUSLEMOONA.\nAnd Allah has made for you of what He has created shelters, and He has given you in the mountains places of retreat, and He has given you garments to preserve you from the heat and coats of mail to preserve you in your fighting; even thus does He complete His favor upon you, that haply you may submit.\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(82)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FA-INNAMAA A’LAYKA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nBut if they turn back, then on you devolves only the clear deliverance (of the message).\nيَعْرِفُوْنَ نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يُنْكِرُوْنَهَا وَاَكْثَرُهُمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(83)\nYA’REFOONA NEA’MATAL LAAHE SUMMA YUNKEROONAHAA WAAKSARUHUMU KAAFEROON.\nThey recognize the favor of Allah, yet they deny it, and most of them are ungrateful.\nوَيَوْمَ نَبْعَثُ مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِيْدًا ثُمَّ لَا يُؤْذَنُ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَلَا هُمْ يُسْتَعْتَبُوْنَ‏(84)\nWA YAWMA NABA’ASU MIN KULLE UMMATIN SHAHEEDAA SUMMA LAA YUZANU LILLAZEENA KAFAROO WA LAA HUM HUM YUSTA’TABOON.\nAnd on the day when We will raise up a witness out of every nation, then shall no permission be given to those who disbelieve, nor shall they be made to solicit favor.\nوَاِذَا رَاَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الْعَذَابَ فَلَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA EZAA RAAALLAZEENA ZALAMOOA A’ZAABA FALAA YOKHAFFAFO A’NHUM WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nAnd when those who are unjust shall see the chastisement, it shall not be lightened for them, nor shall they be respited.\nوَ اِذَا رَاَ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا شُرَكَآءَهُمْ قَالُوْا رَبَّنَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ شُرَكَآؤُنَا الَّذِيْنَ كُنَّا نَدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِكَ‌ۚ فَاَلْقَوْا اِلَيْهِمُ الْقَوْلَ اِنَّكُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(86)\nWA EZAA RAAALLAZEENA ASHRAKOO SHURAKAAAHUM QAALOO RABBANAA HAAOOLAAA-E SHURAKAAUNAA LAZEENA KUNNAA NADU’OOA MIN DOONEKA FAALQAWA ELAYHEMUS QAWLA INNAKUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nAnd when those who associate (others with Allah) shall see their associate-gods, they shall say: Our Lord, these are our associate-gods on whom we called besides Thee. But they will give them back the reply: Most surely you are liars.\nوَاَلْقَوْا اِلَى اللّٰهِ يَوْمَئِذٍ ۨالسَّلَمَ‌ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(87)\nWAALQAWA ELAL LAAHE YAWMA-EZIN AS-SALAMA WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nAnd they shall tender submission to Allah on that day; and what they used to forge shall depart from them.\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ زِدْنٰهُمْ عَذَابًا فَوْقَ الْعَذَابِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يُفْسِدُوْنَ‏(88)\nLAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE ZEDNAAHUM A’ZAABAN FAWQA A’ZAABE BEMAA KAANOO YUFSEDOONA.\n(As for) those who disbelieve and turn away from Allah's way, We will add chastisement to their chastisement because they made mischief.\nوَيَوْمَ نَبْعَثُ فِىْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِيْدًا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِهِمْ‌ وَجِئْنَا بِكَ شَهِيْدًا عَلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ‌ؕ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ تِبْيَانًا لِّكُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّ هُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(89)\nWA YAWMA NABA’ASU FEE KULLE UMMATIN SHAHEEDAA A’LAYHIM MIN ANFOSEHIM WAJENAA BEKA SHAHEEDAA A’LAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA NAZZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABA TEBYAANAN LEKULLE SHAY-IN WA HODAM WA RAHMATAL WA BUSHRAA LIL-MUSLEMEENA.\nAnd on the day when We will raise up in every people a witness against them from among themselves, and bring you as a witness against these-- and We have revealed the Book to you explaining clearly everything, and a guidance and mercy and good news for those who submit.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَاْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْاِحْسَانِ وَاِيْتَآىئِ ذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَيَنْهٰى عَنِ الْفَحْشَآءِ وَالْمُنْكَرِ وَالْبَغْىِ‌ۚ يَعِظُكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(90)\nINNAL LAAHA YAAMURU BIL-A’DL WA EHSAANE WAAYTAAAAE ZIL QURBAA WAYANHAA A’NIL FAHSHAAA-E WAL MUNKARE WAL BAGHAAE YA-E’ZOKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nSurely Allah enjoins the doing of justice and the doing of good (to others) and the giving to the kindred, and He forbids indecency and evil and rebellion; He admonishes you that you may be mindful.\nوَ اَوْفُوْا بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ اِذَا عَاهَدتُّمْ وَلَا تَنْقُضُوا الْاَيْمَانَ بَعْدَ تَوْكِيْدِهَا وَقَدْ جَعَلْتُمُ اللّٰهَ عَلَيْكُمْ كَفِيْلًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(91)\nWA AAWFOOA BEA’AHDE LAAHE EZAA A’AAHADTTUM WA LAA TANQUZOOA AL-AAYMAANA BA’DA TAWKEEDEHAA WA QAD JAA’ALTUMU LAAHA A’LAYKUM KAFEELAN INNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nAnd fulfill the covenant of Allah when you have made a covenant, and do not break the oaths after making them fast, and you have indeed made Allah a surety for you; surely Allah knows what you do.\nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّتِىْ نَقَضَتْ غَزْلَهَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ قُوَّةٍ اَنْكَاثًا ؕ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ اَيْمَانَكُمْ دَخَلًاۢ بَيْنَكُمْ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ اُمَّةٌ هِىَ اَرْبٰى مِنْ اُمَّةٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا يَبْلُوْكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ ‌ؕ وَلَيُبَيِّنَنَّ لَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(92)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO KA-LATEE NAQAZAT GHAZLAHAA MIN BA’DE QUWWATIN AANKAASAN TATTAKHEZOONA AAYMAANAKUM DAKHALAN BAYNAKUM AN TAKOONA UMMATUN HEYA AARBAA MIN UMMATIN INNAMAA YABLOOKUMU LAAHO BEHI WALAYUBAYNANNA LAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE MAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nAnd be not like her who unravels her yarn, disintegrating it into pieces after she has spun it strongly. You make your oaths to be means of deceit between you because (one) nation is more numerous than (another) nation. Allah only tries you by this; and He will most certainly make clear to you on the resurrection day that about which you differed.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَعَلَكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلٰكِنْ يُّضِلُّ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَلَتُسْئَلُنَّ عَمَّا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAA’ALAKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN LAAKIL YYUZELLU MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O WA LA-TUS-A-LUNNA A’MMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd if Allah please He would certainly make you a single nation, but He causes to err whom He pleases and guides whom He pleases; and most certainly you will be questioned as to what you did.\nوَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اَيْمَانَكُمْ دَخَلًاۢ بَيْنَكُمْ فَتَزِلَّ قَدَمٌۢ بَعْدَ ثُبُوْتِهَا وَتَذُوْقُوا السُّوْۤءَ بِمَا صَدَدْتُّمْ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ‌ۚ وَ لَكُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(94)\nWA LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AAYMAANAKUM DAKHALAN BAYNAKUM FATAZELLA QADAMUN BA’DA SUBOOTEHAA WATAZOOQOOA AS-SOOA BEMAA SADADTTUM A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAKUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd do not make your oaths a means of deceit between you, lest a foot should slip after its stability and you should taste evil because you turned away from Allah's way and grievous punishment be your (lot).\nوَلَا تَشْتَرُوْا بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA LAA TASHTAROO BEA’AHDE LAAHE SAMANAN QALEELAA INNAMAA I’NDAL LAAHE HOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nAnd do not take a small price in exchange for Allah's covenant; surely what is with Allah is better for you, did you but know.\nمَا عِنْدَكُمْ يَنْفَدُ‌ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ بَاقٍؕ وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْۤا اَجْرَهُمْ بِاَحْسَنِ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(96)\nMAA E’ENDAKUM YANFADU WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE BAAQIN WALANAJZEENNA LAZEENA SABAROO AJRAHUM BE-AHSANE MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhat is with you passes away and what is with Allah is enduring; and We will most certainly give to those who are patient their reward for the best of what they did.\nمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَنُحْيِيَنَّهٗ حَيٰوةً طَيِّبَةً‌ ۚ وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّهُمْ اَجْرَهُمْ بِاَحْسَنِ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(97)\nMAN A’MELA SAALEHAN MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FALANUHYEENNAH HAYWTAN TAYBATAN WA LANAJZEYANNAHUM AJRAHUM BE-AHSANE MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhoever does good whether male or female and he is a believer, We will most certainly make him live a happy life, and We will most certainly give them their reward for the best of what they did.\nفَاِذَا قَرَاْتَ الْقُرْاٰنَ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ الرَّجِيْمِ‏(98)\nFA-EZAA QARAATA QURAANA FAS-TA-I’Z BIL-LAAHE MENAL SHAYTAANE AR-RAJEEME.\nSo when you recite the Quran, seek refuge with Allah from the accursed Shaitan,\nاِنَّهٗ لَيْسَ لَهٗ سُلْطٰنٌ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ‏(99)\nINNAHU LAYSA LAHU SULTAANUN A’LAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nSurely he has no authority over those who believe and rely on their Lord.\nاِنَّمَا سُلْطٰنُهٗ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَتَوَلَّوْنَهٗ وَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِهٖ مُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(100)\nINNAMAA SULTAANUH A’LAL LAZEENA YATAWALLAWNAH WAL LAZEENA HUM BEHI MUSHREKOONA.\nHis authority is only over those who befriend him and those who associate others with Him.\nوَاِذَا بَدَّلْنَاۤ اٰيَةً مَّكَانَ اٰيَةٍ‌ۙ وَّ اللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يُنَزِّلُ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُفْتَرٍؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(101)\nWA EZAA BAD-DALNAA AAYATAL MMAKAANA AAYATIM WA LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YUNAZZELU QAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MUFTARIN BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd when We change (one) communication for (another) communication, and Allah knows best what He reveals, they say: You are only a forger. Nay, most of them do not know.\nقُلْ نَزَّلَهٗ رُوْحُ الْقُدُسِ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ بِالْحَقِّ لِيُثَبِّتَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَهُدًى وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(102)\nQUL NAZZALAHU ROOHU AL-QUDUSE MIN RABBEKA BIL-HAQQE LEESABBETA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA HODANW WA BUSHRAA LIL-MUSLEMEENA.\nSay: The Holy spirit has revealed it from your Lord with the truth, that it may establish those who believe and as a guidance and good news for those who submit.\nوَلَقَدْ نَعْلَمُ اَنَّهُمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِنَّمَا يُعَلِّمُهٗ بَشَرٌ‌ؕ لِسَانُ الَّذِىْ يُلْحِدُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ اَعْجَمِىٌّ وَّهٰذَا لِسَانٌ عَرَبِىٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(103)\nWA LAQAD NA’LAMO ANNAHUM YAQOOLOONA INNAMAA YUA’ALLEMUH BASHARUN LESAANU LAZEE YULHEDOONA ELAYHE AAA’JAMEAAAUN WWAHAAZAA LESAANUN A’ARABEAAAUN MOBEEN.\nAnd certainly We know that they say: Only a mortal teaches him. The tongue of him whom they reproach is barbarous, and this is clear Arabic tongue.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِۙ لَا يَهْدِيْهِمُ اللّٰهُ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(104)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE LAA YAHDEEHEMU LAAHO WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\n(As for) those who do not believe in Allah's communications, surely Allah will not guide them, and they shall have a painful punishment.\nاِنَّمَا يَفْتَرِى الْكَذِبَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ‌ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(105)\nINNAMAA YAFTAREAA AL-KAZEBA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL AL-KAAZEBOONA.\nOnly they forge the lie who do not believe in Allah's communications, and these are the liars.\nمَنْ كَفَرَ بِاللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اِيْمَانِهٖۤ اِلَّا مَنْ اُكْرِهَ وَقَلْبُهٗ مُطْمَئِنٌّۢ بِالْاِيْمَانِ وَلٰكِنْ مَّنْ شَرَحَ بِالْكُفْرِ صَدْرًا فَعَلَيْهِمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ‌ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(106)\nMAN KAFARA BIL-LAAHE MIN BA’DE AEEMAANEH ILLAA MAN AUKREHA WAQALBUH MUTMAENNUN BIL-EEMAANE WA LAAKIL MAN SHARAHA BIL-KUFRE SADRAN FA A’LAYHIM GHAZABUN MENAL LAAHE WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nHe who disbelieves in Allah after his having believed, not he who is compelled while his heart is at rest on account of faith, but he who opens (his) breast to disbelief-- on these is the wrath of Allah, and they shall have a grievous chastisement.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمُ اسْتَحَبُّوا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا عَلَى الْاٰخِرَةِ ۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(107)\nZAA LEKA BEAANNAHUMU ASTAHABBOOA HAYAATAD DUNYAA A’LAL AAKHERATE WA ANNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ KAAFEREEN.\nThis is because they love this world's life more than the hereafter, and because Allah does not guide the unbelieving people.\nاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ طَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَسَمْعِهِمْ وَاَبْصَارِهِمْ‌ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْغٰفِلُوْنَ‏(108)\nAOOLAAEKA LAZEENA TABAA’A LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM WASAME’EHEM WA ABSAAREHIM WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL AL-GHAAFELOONA.\nThese are they on whose hearts and their hearing and their eyes Allah has set a seal, and these are the heedless ones.\nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(109)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAHUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nNo doubt that in the hereafter they will be the losers.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا فُتِنُوْا ثُمَّ جٰهَدُوْا وَصَبَرُوْۤا ۙ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(110)\nSUMMA INNAL RABBAKA LILLAZEENA HAAJAROO MIN BA’DE MAA FUTENOOA SUMMA JAAHADOOA WA SABAROO INNAL RABBAKA MIN BAA’DEHAA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nYet surely your Lord, with respect to those who fly after they are persecuted, then they struggle hard and are patient, most surely your Lord after that is Forgiving, Merciful.\nيَوْمَ تَاْتِىْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ تُجَادِلُ عَنْ نَّفْسِهَا وَتُوَفّٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(111)\nYAWMA TAATEAA KULLO NAFSIM TUJAADELU A’N NNAFSEHAA WA TOWAFFAA KULLO NAFSIM MAA A’MELAT WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\n(Remember) the day when every soul shall come, pleading for itself and every soul shall be paid in full what it has done, and they shall not be dealt with unjustly.\nوَضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا قَرْيَةً كَانَتْ اٰمِنَةً مُّطْمَئِنَّةً يَّاْتِيْهَا رِزْقُهَا رَغَدًا مِّنْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ فَكَفَرَتْ بِاَنْعُمِ اللّٰهِ فَاَذَاقَهَا اللّٰهُ لِبَاسَ الْجُوْعِ وَالْخَوْفِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(112)\nWA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAA QARYATAN KAANAT AAAMENATAN MMUTMAENNATAN YYAATEEHAA REZQUHAA RAGHADAN MIN KULLE MAKAANIN FAKAFARAT BEAANU’UME LAAHE FAAZAAQAHAA LAAHO LEBAASA AL-JOOE’E WA KHAWFE BEMAA KAANOO YASNAU’OONA.\nAnd Allah sets forth a parable: (Consider) a town safe and secure to which its means of subsistence come in abundance from every quarter; but it became ungrateful to Allah's favors, therefore Allah made it to taste the utmost degree of hunger and fear because of what they wrought.\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَهُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(113)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUM MINHUM FA-KAZZABOOHO TOOFAANO A’ZAABO WA HUM ZAALEMOON.\nAnd certainly there came to them an Apostle from among them, but they rejected him, so the punishment overtook them while they were unjust.\nفَكُلُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ حَلٰلًا طَيِّبًا وَّاشْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(114)\nFA-KOLOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO HALAALAN TAYYEBAA WWAASHKUROOA NEA’MATAL LAAHE IN KUNTUM IYYAAHO TA’BODOONA.\nTherefore eat of what Allah has given you, lawful and good (things), and give thanks for Allah's favor if Him do you serve.\nاِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةَ وَ الدَّمَ وَلَحْمَ الْخِنْزِيْرِ وَمَاۤ اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖ‌ۚ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ غَيْرَ بَاغٍ وَّلَا عَادٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(115)\nINNAMAA HARRAMA A’LAYKOMUL MAYTATA WA AD-DAMA WA LAHMAL KHINZEERE WA MAA OHILLA LE-GHAYRIL LAAHE BEHI FAMANE’ TURRA GHAYRA BAAGHINW WA LAA A’ADIN FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nHe has only forbidden you what dies of itself and blood and flesh of swine and that over which any other name than that of Allah has been invoked, but whoever is driven to necessity, not desiring nor exceeding the limit, then surely Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا لِمَا تَصِفُ اَلْسِنَتُكُمُ الْكَذِبَ هٰذَا حَلٰلٌ وَّهٰذَا حَرَامٌ لِّتَفْتَرُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ‌ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ لَا يُفْلِحُوْنَؕ‏(116)\nWA LAA TAQOOLOO LEMAKH TASEFU AALSENATUKUMU AL-KAZEBA HAAZAA HALAALUN WWAHAAZAA HARAAMUN LLETAFTAROOA A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA INNAL LAZEENA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA LAA YUFLEHOONA.\nAnd, for what your tongues describe, do not utter the lie, (saying) This is lawful and this is unlawful, in order to forge a lie against Allah; surely those who forge the lie against Allah shall not prosper.\nمَتَاعٌ قَلِيْلٌ وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(117)\nLIL-MOTAALLAQAATE QALEELUN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nA little enjoyment and they shall have a painful punishment.\nوَعَلَى الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا حَرَّمْنَا مَا قَصَصْنَا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ‌ۚ وَمَا ظَلَمْنٰهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(118)\nWA LAZEENA HAADOO HARRAMNAA MAA QASASNAA A’LAYKA MIN QABLO WA MAA ZALAMNAAHUM WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nAnd for those who were Jews We prohibited what We have related to you already, and We did them no injustice, but they were unjust to themselves.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِيْنَ عَمِلُوا السُّوْۤءَ بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ تَابُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ وَاَصْلَحُوْۤا ۙ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(119)\nSUMMA INNAL RABBAKA LILLAZEENA A’MELUS AS-SOOA BEJAHAALATIN SUMMA TAABOO MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA WA ASLAHOO INNAL RABBAKA MIN BAA’DEHAA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nYet surely your Lord, with respect to those who do an evil in ignorance, then turn after that and make amends, most surely your Lord after that is Forgiving, Merciful.\nاِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ كَانَ اُمَّةً قَانِتًا لِّلَّهِ حَنِيْفًاؕ وَلَمْ يَكُ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَۙ‏(120)\nINNAL IBRAAHEEMA KAANA UMMATAM QAANETAN LILLAAH HANEEFAN WA LAM YAKU MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSurely Ibrahim was an exemplar, obedient to Allah, upright, and he was not of the polytheists.\nشَاكِرًا لِّاَنْعُمِهِ‌ؕ اِجْتَبٰٮهُ وَهَدٰٮهُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(121)\nSHAAKERAWN LEAANU’UMEHE AEJTABAAHU WAHADAAHU ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nGrateful for His favors; He chose him and guided him on the right path.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُ فِى الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً‌  ؕ وَاِنَّهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَؕ‏(122)\nWA AATAYNAAHO FIL DUNYAA HASANATANW WA INNAHU FIL AAKHERATE LAMENAS AS-SAALEHEENA.\nAnd We gave him good in this world, and in the next he will most surely be among the good.\nثُمَّ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ اَنِ اتَّبِعْ مِلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(123)\nSUMMA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA SAALEHAN ATTABEA’ MILLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nThen We revealed to you: Follow the faith of Ibrahim, the upright one, and he was not of the polytheists.\nاِنَّمَا جُعِلَ السَّبْتُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(124)\nINNAMAA JUE’ELA AS-SABTU A’LAL LAZEENA TALAFOO FEEH WA INNA RABBAKA LAYAHKUMU BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nThe Sabbath was ordained only for those who differed about it, and most surely your Lord will judge between them on the resurrection day concerning that about which they differed.\nاُدْعُ اِلٰى سَبِيْلِ رَبِّكَ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَالْمَوْعِظَةِ الْحَسَنَةِ‌ وَجَادِلْهُمْ بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ‌ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(125)\nAUDU’U ELAA SABEELIL RABBEKA BIL-HEKMATE WAL MAWE’EZATE HASANATE WAJAADELHUM BIL-LATEE HEYA AAHSANU INNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAN ZALLA A’N SABEELEH WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BILMOHTADEEN.\nCall to the way of your Lord with wisdom and goodly exhortation, and have disputations with them in the best manner; surely your Lord best knows those who go astray from His path, and He knows best those who follow the right way.\nوَاِنْ عَاقَبْتُمْ فَعَاقِبُوْا بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوْقِبْتُمْ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَلَئِنْ صَبَرْتُمْ لَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لِّلصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(126)\nWA A’AAQABTUM FAA’AAQEBOOA BE-MISLE MAA U’OOQEBTUM BEHI WA LAIN SABARTUM LAHOWAL KHAYRUL LLELSSAABEREENA.\nAnd if you take your turn, then retaliate with the like of that with which you were afflicted; but if you are patient, it will certainly be best for those who are patient.\nوَاصْبِرْ وَمَا صَبْرُكَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ‌ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا تَكُ فِىْ ضَيْقٍ مِّمَّا يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(127)\nWAS BIR WA MAA SABRUKA ILLAA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA TAHZAN A’LAYHIM WA LAA TAKU FEE ZAYQIM MIMMAA YAMKOROON.\nAnd be patient and your patience is not but by (the assistance of) Allah, and grieve not for them, and do not distress yourself at what they plan.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا وَّالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مُّحْسِنُوْنَ‏(128)\nINNAL LAAHA LAAHA LAZEENA TAQAW WWAALLAZEENA HUM MMUHSENOONA.\nSurely Allah is with those who guard (against evil) and those who do good (to others).",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has 128 ayaat. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is recorded from the Holy Prophet (S) that whoever recites this Surah will not be questioned, on the Day of Judgement, about the blessings he received on the Earth and will get the reward equal to the amount of people who left a good will when they died.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites Surah an-Nahl once every month, he will be safe from 70 types of diseases and will be from among the people of Jannah. This Surah should, however, under no circumstance be written and kept in the house or garden as it may have harmful effects. Imam Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if kept in a house or garden, it will soon be destroyed. Indeed this is a weapon that one is only allowed to use against an evil person who is the enemy of Islam."
}
